# The working tree uses LF on every platform.
#
# public/_headers pins Content-Security-Policy hashes for the page's one inline
# script and one inline style block, and a CSP hash is taken over the exact bytes
# between the tags. A CRLF checkout changes those bytes and so changes the hash,
# which would block the page's own script in the browser with nothing in the page
# to say why. Pinning eol=lf keeps the hash the same wherever the file is read.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
